 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/36f36cd5ece4186095afcf2ffbfb7b80cc04b6c2e3226e7477a419a9fbc96f85.png] **__Key Points__**

__

• **Dreamweaver** is a web development tool rather than a desktop publishing software.



• Dreamweaver is used for designing, coding, and managing websites and web applications.

• It provides a visual interface along with a code editor for HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and other web technologies.

• Dreamweaver includes features like live preview, syntax highlighting, and code completion.

• It supports various web standards and frameworks, making it a versatile tool for web development.



 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/f13e2ad6582c16aa62a83672e2547ad20a01fddb61962a1acce42eb9a1a99caa.png] **Additional Information__**


• Dreamweaver integrates with other Adobe tools, enhancing its capabilities for web design and development.

• It offers features like version control, FTP client, and compatibility with multiple browsers.

• Dreamweaver is suitable for both beginners and experienced developers due to its user-friendly interface and advanced features.

• It supports responsive design, allowing developers to create websites that work well on various devices and screen sizes.

